Module hhg "The House That Grows" {
  Description "Act III. The downhill end of the Long Hall, where the knocking is: the keeper of the Slope and her lamp, the Reckoning on the wall, a gate with two locks, a front door nobody has used, and the girl who has been knocking at it from the inside.".

  // The count the house is keeping is the Seventh's age in rooms; its first page (why a girl of fourteen was left to dream
  // a house for two and a half thousand years) is missing and is never read out. The price of reading it is that
  // whoever answers the knocking becomes the next to be asked.

  // ---- Places ----
  Place slope "the Slope" is room within decks at 0, 2 indoors.
  Place front_hall "the front hall" is room within decks at 0, 3 indoors.
  Place the_sill "the sill of the front door" is room within keel at 2, 3 outdoors.
  // The Long Hall runs downhill to the Slope on its own floor: the one way in the house that is not a dream-door, which
  // is why the knocking can always be heard from it.
  Passage hall_slope "the downhill end of the Long Hall" is passage between long_hall and slope.
  Passage front_gate "the gate at the foot of the Slope" is door between slope and front_hall.
  Passage front_door "the front door of the house" is door between front_hall and the_sill.

  Observe slope_scene at slope as fixture when true "The Long Hall's floor tilts here until it is a ramp for carts, and then a chute, glass worn to the shine of a spoon. Warm air comes up it from below, and with the air the smell of hot lamp-oil, and the knocking: eleven knocks, close, quick, and then a long wait of the exact length of the eleven, and then eleven again. At the foot a gate of green glass barred with brass stands shut. A lamp burns beside it.".
  Observe hall_slope_back at slope as feature when true "Behind you the Long Hall goes up and away, forty doors on each hand, all shut, none of them looking at you.".
  Observe front_hall_scene at front_hall as fixture when true "A porch the size of a barn, with one door in it: a plain front door of dark house-timber, the only wood in the whole house, with a brass knocker in the shape of a hand and three steps up to a threshold worn hollow by feet that never came. The knocking comes from the near side of it. On the wall are hooks for outdoor coats. The hooks are empty, every one.".
  Observe sill_scene at the_sill as fixture when true "A step of raw stone outside the front door, bolted to the underside of the Keel: nothing in front of it but a very long drop, the cloud of the Veil, and Cobble Ring's pond shining at the bottom of the air like a dropped coin.".

  // ---- Sabe Orrel, and the kept light ----
  Person sabe "Sabe Orrel" at slope {
    Role "keeper of the Slope, a Lifted woman of seventy who minds a lamp". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner stoic.
    Likeness "midwife".
    Greets "A small old woman in a Netters' harness gone grey with age sits on an upturned bucket with a lamp on the floor between her feet and her back against the gate. She does not look round. 'Don't open it,' she says. 'And don't sit on the floor, it slides. There's tea in the can, if the can's still hot, and if it isn't it's been a long day.'".
  }
  Thing sabe_lamp "the keeper's lamp" at slope {
    State lit "A lamp of selm-glass the size of a pear burns on the floor beside the bucket: a small steady flame the colour of pond-ice, that does not move when the knocking comes. Under the foot, scratched small, a name: WENN.".
  }
  Initially Assert state(sabe_lamp, lit).
  // She wants the knocking to stop in her lifetime; she is afraid of being the one who stopped it; she says she only minds
  // the lamp; pressed, she will put the lamp out for you.
  Topic sabe_lamp_why with sabe "Ask Sabe whom the lamp is lit for" when true once {
    Says "'Wenn,' says Sabe. 'He had the night-watch on this stair when I was a girl. They said he came off it in the morning and I said I'd see.' She turns the lamp a quarter with her foot, the way you turn a pot to the fire. 'I have not seen. Seventy years of not seeing is a long time to mind a lamp. I mind it.'".
  }
  Topic sabe_knock with sabe "Ask Sabe about the knocking" when true once {
    Says "'Eleven,' says Sabe, 'and a gap for the twelfth. Always has been, in my time and my mother's. If you count it out loud somebody counts the twelfth with you, so I don't.' She looks at her knuckles. 'It is a girl, and she is on the inside, and she thinks she is knocking to come in. There is a difference between wanting in and wanting out, and from the inside you can't tell, and from the outside you can't either. Don't you open that gate for the first one you think it is.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, eleven_strokes). }
  }
  Discovery eleven_strokes "The knocking at the front door of the house is eleven knocks and a gap of the same length where the twelfth should be. Whoever is inside has never been answered with the twelfth.".
  Topic sabe_undal with sabe "Ask Sabe whether she can read the Undal letters on the bunk shelves" when not gaveLetter(sabe) {
    Says "'Undal.' Sabe laughs, short. 'It's what the Ballast-Reeve forbids on the nets, so everyone on the nets can read it.' She takes from her harness a square of folded cord-paper, dark with years. 'The Lifted children wrote to their mothers on the shelves and never had a way to send it. I took this one off the end bunk before the glass grew over. It is to the reeve of Cobble Ring from her brother, who was taken up as a Netter in the famine year, and who writes in Undal because he had no one to teach him the other. I can read you it. You can carry it down.'".
    On discuss { Assert gaveLetter(sabe). Give hhg_undal_letter to actor. Assert knows(actor, brother_letter). }
  }
  Relation gaveLetter(group). Relation gaveToken(group). Relation gaveRope(group).
  Discovery brother_letter "Sabe Orrel holds a letter in Undal letters from the reeve of Cobble Ring's brother, taken up to the Keel as a child in the famine year: he writes that the house in the barley is not a thing to sell but a thing to answer, and that the city has no one who knows how.".
  Kind hhg_undal_letter "a Lifted child's letter in Undal" is gear worth 1 described "A square of cord-paper folded small, written in the narrow Undal letters the Ballast-Reeve forbids on the nets, in a child's careful hand; the creases are brown with years of a harness.".
  Item letter "a Lifted child's letter in Undal" is hhg_undal_letter at nowhere owned by sabe.
  Topic sabe_tea with sabe "Ask Sabe about the Netters, Captain Isele, and the Knot House" when true once {
    Says "'The Knot House ties the net, and unties whoever ties wrong,' says Sabe. 'Isele's span has the hatch at the foot of Rigging Row, and she'll hear a knot cut from the wrong side before the rope has stopped swinging. Cut it from the right side, with a Netter, and it's a favour. From below, it's theft.' She sips from the can. 'A rope would help you out along the edge. A Netter's token would help you with Isele.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, knot_custom). }
  }
  Discovery knot_custom "The Knot House treats a knot undone from below as theft; from above, with a Netter, as a favour. A Netters' token, or a paid fee, settles it with Isele's span.".
  Topic sabe_token with sabe "Ask Sabe for a Netters' token, to show Isele" when knows(actor, knot_custom) and not gaveToken(sabe) once {
    Says "Sabe unclips a knotted loop of tarred cord from her harness and puts it in your hand. 'Isele knows my knot,' she says. 'Show it, and say Sabe sent the floor-dirt. She'll swear. She won't strike.'".
    On discuss { Assert gaveToken(sabe). Give sabe_token to actor. }
  }
  Kind hhg_netters_token "a Netters' token" is gear worth 1 described "A loop of tarred cord tied in the knot the Knot House calls a keeper's: it means that the holder is a guest of the span, and that Sabe Orrel has stood for them.".
  Item sabe_token "a Netters' token" is hhg_netters_token at nowhere owned by sabe.
  Topic sabe_rope with sabe "Ask Sabe if she has a rope for the wind along the edge" when knows(actor, knot_custom) and not gaveRope(sabe) once {
    Says "She pulls a hank of Netters' rope from under the bucket, ten fathoms, and does not say where she got it. 'For the edge,' she says. 'Tie off on the bunk-room shelf and walk it. The wind's no worse than it was when I was a girl and no kinder.'".
    On discuss { Assert gaveRope(sabe). Give sabe_rope to actor. }
  }
  Item sabe_rope "ten fathoms of Netters' rope" is rope at nowhere owned by sabe.

  // ---- Voices of the company, by calling ----
  Relation heardShelf(group). Relation heardLamps(group). Relation heardHall(group). Relation heardSlope(group).
  Relation heardSlopeB(group). Relation heardHallB(group). Relation heardGate(group). Relation heardGateB(group).
  Rule voice_monk_shelf at cup_shelf when memberOf(?m, party) and hasCalling(?m, calling_monk) and awake(?m) and at(party, cup_shelf) and not heardShelf(party)
    says "{?m} stands with feet apart and lets the room come to {?m} instead of going to it. 'Twelve cups, and one has the wrong number of cracks,' {?m} says, after a while. 'Don't tell me it's a trick of the light. You learn what a room does when you have looked at it for a long time.'" {
    Assert heardShelf(party).
  }
  Rule voice_thief_lamps at lamp_store when memberOf(?m, party) and hasCalling(?m, calling_thief) and awake(?m) and at(party, lamp_store) and not heardLamps(party)
    says "{?m} lifts a lamp and weighs it, and sets it exactly back in its own dust-ring. 'These aren't stock,' {?m} says. 'Stock gets dusted. These get left. Somebody counts them every year and puts them back as they were.'" {
    Assert heardLamps(party).
  }
  Rule voice_ranger_hall at long_hall when memberOf(?m, party) and hasCalling(?m, calling_ranger) and awake(?m) and at(party, long_hall) and not heardHall(party)
    says "{?m} crouches by a smear of glass dust at the hall's downhill end. 'Bare feet,' {?m} says. 'Small, and sixty years old, and been this way every night this week, down and not back.' {?m} follows the print with a finger. 'Somebody walks in her sleep and she isn't hurrying.'" {
    Assert heardHall(party).
  }
  Rule voice_bard_hall at long_hall when memberOf(?m, party) and hasCalling(?m, calling_bard) and awake(?m) and at(party, long_hall) and not heardHallB(party)
    says "{?m} hums, half a bar, and stops. 'That knocking is in six-eight,' {?m} says. 'Eleven beats and a rest, and the tune wants the rest. I could finish that phrase in my sleep, and I think that is what has been said to everyone who ever stood here.'" {
    Assert heardHallB(party).
  }
  Rule voice_cleric_slope at slope when memberOf(?m, party) and hasCalling(?m, calling_cleric) and awake(?m) and at(party, slope) and not heardSlope(party)
    says "{?m} lays a palm on the glass of the wall, as a priest lays it on a sickbed, and keeps it there through two rounds of the knocking. 'Warm,' {?m} says. 'Not from the lamp. It is warm the way a door is warm when someone has just let go of the handle.'" {
    Assert heardSlope(party).
  }
  Rule voice_warrior_slope at slope when memberOf(?m, party) and hasCalling(?m, calling_warrior) and awake(?m) and at(party, slope) and not heardSlopeB(party)
    says "{?m} stamps once on the glass floor, and listens to what it says. 'This is a ramp for carts,' {?m} says. 'Wide, level, and sloped for a brake. Nobody builds that to bring a child in. They build it to take a thing out.'" {
    Assert heardSlopeB(party).
  }
  Rule voice_thief_gate at slope when memberOf(?m, party) and hasCalling(?m, calling_thief) and awake(?m) and at(party, slope) and not heardGate(party)
    says "{?m} goes down on a knee to the gate's lock and looks at it sideways. 'Two locks,' {?m} says. 'The old one is glass and means to be asked. The brass one is newer, and a thing that is newer than the lock beside it was put on by somebody who was frightened.'" {
    Assert heardGate(party).
  }
  Rule voice_monk_gate at slope when memberOf(?m, party) and hasCalling(?m, calling_monk) and awake(?m) and at(party, slope) and not heardGateB(party)
    says "{?m} stands before the gate with the arms hung loose and does not blink. Behind the glass the knocking slows. 'She is not looking away either,' {?m} says, very quietly. 'We have been staring at each other through a door for as long as you have been here. One of us has to blink, and it will not be her.'" {
    Assert heardGateB(party).
  }

  // ---- The gate: three ways, and each leaves a different girl ----
  Thing gate_leaf "the gate at the foot of the Slope" on front_gate {
    State barred blocking "A gate of green glass barred with a brass bar, shut. The knocking comes through it, eleven and the wait.".
    State open "The gate stands open. Beyond it is the front hall, and the knocking is very near.".
    Change pick "Pick the brass lock of the gate" from barred to open needing lockwork.
  }
  Initially Assert state(gate_leaf, barred).
  Relation gateForced(group). Relation gateAnswered(group). Relation gateStared(group).
  Rule gate_forced_known when state(gate_leaf, open) and not gateAnswered(party) and not gateStared(party) { Assert gateForced(party). }
  // The honest way: knock the eleven, and wait, and the twelfth comes from inside, because someone outside has answered.
  Action knock_count(actor: group, site: place) "Knock the eleven at the gate, and wait the length of the twelfth" {
    Description "Eleven knocks and the wait. The gate is asked, not forced.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, slope) and state(gate_leaf, barred) and knows(actor, eleven_strokes).
    Time 3.
    On success { Assert state(gate_leaf, open). Assert gateAnswered(party). }
    Result "You knock eleven, in her time, and wait in the gap. In the gap, from the other side of the glass, a twelfth knock comes: small, and a little late, and the glass sighs as the brass bar lifts itself clear. 'Oh,' says a voice behind the gate, in the voice of a girl who has been fourteen for two and a half thousand years. 'You waited.'".
  }
  // The monk's way (and the stare-trained's): look at the gate until it blinks. It is the one door that opens in front of its watcher.
  Action stare_gate(actor: group, site: place, m: member) "Stare at the gate with {m} until the brass bar lets go" {
    Description "A Watch-trained eye can outhold a girl who has had two and a half thousand years to practise. It takes an hour, and nobody must look away.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, slope) and state(gate_leaf, barred) and stareTrained(actor)
      and memberOf(m, actor) and hasCalling(m, calling_monk) and awake(m) and companyLooks(actor, site).
    Time 6. Interrupted when not companyLooks(actor, site).
    On success { Assert state(gate_leaf, open). Assert gateStared(party). }
    Result "You do not blink. {m} does not blink. Somewhere behind the glass a girl sets her jaw and does not blink either, for a very long time, and then the brass bar drops its latch with a sound like someone sitting down, and a small voice says, aggrieved, 'That isn't fair, you've done it before.'".
  }
  // The Netters' rope across the edge to the sill is the way a visitor from outside comes to the front door: it takes the front way.
  Passage edge_to_sill "the ledge along the Keel to the sill" is crawl between keel_edge and the_sill.
  Thing sill_wind "the wind along the ledge" on edge_to_sill is scenery {
    State blowing dangerous "The wind along the Keel's underside would take a person off a ledge as wide as a hand.".
    State slack "The wind along the ledge has dropped to nothing.".
    Hurts with keel_fall when blowing then slack.
  }
  Initially Assert state(sill_wind, blowing).
  Rule sill_wind_drops when state(sill_wind, blowing) and untilLight(clock) == 3 { Assert state(sill_wind, slack). }
  Rule sill_wind_rises when state(sill_wind, slack) and untilLight(clock) == 1 { Assert state(sill_wind, blowing). }

  // ---- Neme, behind the gate ----
  Person neme "Neme" at front_hall {
    Role "the Seventh, a girl of fourteen, who has dreamed a house for two and a half thousand years". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner jovial.
    Likeness "child".
    Greets "A girl of fourteen in a coat with the collar torn and a name stitched on it stands with her back to the front door and one hand lifted for a knock she is not giving. 'Don't look at me like that,' she says. 'I know it's rude. Everybody always does. I'm only knocking to see who answers.'".
  }
  Initially Assert at(neme, nowhere).
  Rule neme_there when state(gate_leaf, open) and at(neme, nowhere) { Retract at(neme, nowhere). Assert at(neme, front_hall). }
  Relation nemeTrusts(group). Relation nemeFree(group). Relation nemeSits(group). Relation nemeLeft(group).
  Topic neme_who with neme "Ask Neme who she is" when true once {
    Says "'Neme,' she says, 'and the Seventh, they say, but I can't count that high.' She scuffs a toe along the threshold. 'I asked a woman to look away once, in a field. She did. I didn't think she would, and then I couldn't stop looking at what she'd let go of. I don't want anyone to be sorry. I only want one person to come in the way a person comes in. By the door.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, neme_asked). }
  }
  Discovery neme_asked "Neme asked Kezu, across a night of staring, to look away and let the little door open, because no one has ever come into her house by the front door.".
  Topic neme_knock with neme "Ask Neme why she knocks eleven and not twelve" when true once {
    Says "'Because it isn't polite to do all the knocking,' says Neme, as if you were being slow.".
  }
  Topic neme_marble with neme "Ask Neme about the coat with her name on it, and the orange marble" when knows(actor, door_opened) {
    Says "Neme looks at her collar. 'It's got a name on it because I kept losing it,' she says. 'I put the marble in the pocket so I could find the coat. It's a bad system.' She laughs, once. 'If you've got the marble, I'd like it back.'".
  }
  Relation marbleBack(group).
  Action give_marble(actor: group, site: place) "Give Neme the orange-glass marble from her coat" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(neme, site) and carries(actor, marble) and not nemeTrusts(party).
    On success { Spend marble from actor. Assert nemeTrusts(party). Assert marbleBack(party). }
    Result "She holds it up to the grey light and squints through it, and for a moment the whole front hall is the colour of weak tea. 'There,' she says. 'Now I know where I am.' She does not say thank you. She puts it in her pocket with a kind of savagery, and stands a little straighter, and you understand that you have just been trusted with something.".
  }
  Rule neme_trusts_by_answer when gateAnswered(party) and at(neme, front_hall) and not nemeTrusts(party) { Assert nemeTrusts(party). }

  // ---- The choice at the front door: three answers, each of which costs something ----
  Relation tobuChair(group).
  // 1. Open the door, with her, and take her out into the Strewnfield. The house, finished, stops growing; Kezu sleeps.
  Action let_neme_out(actor: group, site: place) "Take Neme's hand, open the front door, and walk out by it with her" {
    Description "No one has ever come into the house by its front door. This is the first to go out of it.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, front_hall) and at(neme, front_hall) and state(gate_leaf, open) and nemeTrusts(party) and not nemeFree(party) and not nemeSits(party) and not nemeLeft(party).
    Time 2.
    On success { Assert nemeFree(party). Retract doorIn(kezu_bed). Retract sleepwalking(kezu). Assert at(neme, the_sill). Assert state(sill_wind, slack). Assert at(party, the_sill). }
    Result "The door opens outward, which it has never done. The wind comes in smelling of pond and barley, and Neme steps onto the sill in her torn coat with her chin up, and holds your hand a great deal harder than you expected. Below you, a very long way, a ring of houses faces a pond, and in every one a watcher in a loft turns, one after another, to look up. Behind you the house breathes out, and for the first time in its life stops growing.".
  }
  // 2. Ask Tobu to sit the chair for good, and leave the girl her house: the watcher's price.
  Action tobu_takes_chair(actor: group, site: place) "Ask Tobu to go up and take the child's chair for good, and tell Neme she may go" {
    Description "A watched house does not grow. A watcher in the chair is a watcher for good.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, front_hall) and at(neme, front_hall) and state(gate_leaf, open) and nemeTrusts(party) and following(tobu, actor) and not nemeFree(party) and not nemeSits(party) and not nemeLeft(party).
    Time 3.
    On success { Assert nemeSits(party). Assert tobuChair(party). Assert watcher(tobu). Retract following(tobu, actor). Assert at(tobu, long_hall). Assert sitting(tobu). Retract doorIn(kezu_bed). Retract sleepwalking(kezu). Assert at(neme, the_sill). Assert at(party, the_sill). }
    Result "Tobu hears out the whole of it with his hands in his coat, and says, 'Eleven coat-hooks. I counted them a hundred times.' He goes up the Slope without looking back, and in a little while the knocking stops, and the front door swings out on a morning it has never seen, and Neme goes down the stone steps with her hand in yours. Somewhere up in the Long Hall, in a chair the right size for someone small, a young man from Cobble Ring has begun to count doors.".
  }
  // 3. Shut the gate on her and go: the house stays as it was, and goes on.
  Action leave_the_gate(actor: group, site: place) "Shut the gate again, and leave Neme to her knocking" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, front_hall) and at(neme, front_hall) and not nemeFree(party) and not nemeSits(party) and not nemeLeft(party).
    Time 1.
    On success { Assert nemeLeft(party). Assert state(gate_leaf, barred). Assert at(party, slope). }
    Result "You tell her you will come back. She says, quite kindly, 'They all say that,' and turns round to face her door. The gate closes behind you on its own, and the brass bar drops, and after a little while, from behind it, the knocking begins again: eleven, and the wait.".
  }

  // ---- The letter, and the vote ----
  Entity letter_read: fact "the brother's letter".
  Action give_letter_reeve(actor: group, site: place) "Give the reeve the Lifted brother's letter, with Sabe's reading of it" {
    Description "The reeve has not heard from her brother since the famine year. The letter is not about the sale; it changes how the sale feels.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(tessa, site) and holding(actor, hhg_undal_letter)
      and not voted(tessa) and not persuaded(tessa, letter_read) and sellVotes(tessa) >= 2.
    On success { Spend hhg_undal_letter from actor. Assert persuaded(tessa, letter_read). Decrease sellVotes(tessa) by 2. }
    Result "The reeve reads it standing, with her lips moving on the Undal, which she taught herself from a child's primer in the year he went. She reads it twice. Then she goes to the window, and stands there with her back to you for a time. 'He says it's a thing to be answered,' she says at last. 'Not a thing to be sold.' She does not turn round. 'Four arcs for selling. I'll have to speak to the other five.'".
  }

  // ---- The Knot House: a fight is possible and costly; there are two ways round ----
  Person riggers "the Knot House riggers" at nowhere {
    Role "three Netters in harness, with belaying-pins, sent down to find who cut the knot". Ancestry human. Calling warrior. Level 2. Numbers 3. Pronouns they.
    Temperament proud.
    Warns "Three Netters in harness come along the net toward the hatch with belaying-pins in their hands, and the one in front says, quite loudly, 'Floor-dirt. Cut a knot from the wrong side. That's a hand, in the Knot House, or a fee, or the ledge.' Another adds, 'Isele wants a word. She says it would be a short one.'".
    Pleads "The riggers drop their pins on the net and put their hands up, one of them holding on to a stay with his teeth.".
  }
  Initially Set tribute(riggers) to 4.
  Rule riggers_come when knotBroken(rigging_foot) and at(party, rigging_foot) and at(riggers, nowhere) and not riggersSettled(party) { Retract at(riggers, nowhere). Assert at(riggers, rigging_foot). }
  Relation riggersSettled(group).
  Action show_token(actor: group, site: place) "Show the riggers Sabe Orrel's knot, and say that Sabe sent you" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, rigging_foot) and at(riggers, rigging_foot) and holding(actor, hhg_netters_token) and not riggersSettled(party).
    Time 1 minutes.
    On success { Assert riggersSettled(party). Assert tolerates(riggers, actor). Assert at(riggers, nowhere). }
    Result "The one in front takes the tarred loop, turns it in the light, and swears, at length and without repeating herself. 'That's Sabe's,' she says. 'That's Sabe's own keeper's.' She gives it back as if it were hot. 'Isele will have a word anyway. It will be a different one.' They go back along the net with their pins hanging, and one of them looks over his shoulder at you the whole way.".
  }
  Action pay_knot_fee(actor: group, site: place) "Pay the riggers four coin for the knot, to the Knot House's purse" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, rigging_foot) and at(riggers, rigging_foot) and quantity(actor, gold) >= 4 and not riggersSettled(party).
    Time 1 minutes.
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 4. Increase quantity(riggers, gold) by 4. Assert riggersSettled(party). Assert tolerates(riggers, actor). Assert at(riggers, nowhere). }
    Result "The tall rigger counts the coin twice, bites one, and hands it to the youngest, who puts it in a purse with a knot on it. 'Fee paid,' she says. 'That's the knot. The cutting's another matter, but Isele doesn't take cuttings from a fee-payer on a Monday.' They go back along the net, not hurrying.".
  }

  Observe neme_forced at front_hall as feature when gateForced(party) and at(neme, front_hall) and not nemeTrusts(party) "Neme stands very straight with her hand lifted for a knock, and does not look at you. 'You did not wait,' she says. 'Everyone is always so quick.'".
  Milestone m_keeper "found the keeper of the Slope and heard the knocking counted" worth 100 when knows(party, eleven_strokes).
  Milestone m_brother "carried a Lifted brother's letter to the reeve of Cobble Ring" worth 150 when persuaded(tessa, letter_read).
  Milestone m_gate "opened the gate at the foot of the Slope" worth 150 when state(gate_leaf, open).
  Milestone m_marble "gave Neme back her marble" worth 100 when marbleBack(party).
  Milestone m_out "walked Neme out by the front door" worth 400 when nemeFree(party).
  Milestone m_chair "let Tobu take the chair so that Neme might go" worth 300 when nemeSits(party).
  Milestone m_riggers "settled the Knot House's riggers without a blow" worth 100 when riggersSettled(party).

  // ---- The four acts, told as chapters ----
  Chapter ch_ring "I. Cobble Ring" when at(party, ?p) and within(party, ring) and not knows(party, door_opened) "Cobble Ring keeps itself awake. Every house on the rim has a loft with a shutter, and in every loft someone is sitting up with something: a sick cow, a sleeping sister, a hole in the barley. It is how the town has lived on this plain since before the Veil came down, and it has never once been asked what the watching is for.".
  Chapter ch_barley "II. The House in the Barley" when at(party, ?p) and houseRoom(?p) and not keelSide(?p) "Here the law is plain: what is watched is fixed, and what is not, grows. The house is a country with a bedroom the size of a barn, and the town sits round it on stools, afraid of its own yawns.".
  Chapter ch_keel "III. The Keel" when at(party, ?p) and keelSide(?p) "Up here the house is not a room but a city's underside, and the Long Hall has been dreamed for two and a half thousand years by someone who is not tired.".
  Chapter ch_slope "IV. The Slope" when at(party, slope) or at(party, front_hall) "At the foot of the Long Hall the floor tilts, the knocking is loud, and an old woman minds a lamp for someone who is not coming. There is only one door left, and the whole house is built to keep you from using it.".

  // ---- Two further links outward, and a comic scene in a grave house ----
  Topic dace_exchange with dace "Ask Dace where the Company sends what falls out of the city" when true once {
    Says "'The Founders' Exchange sells it on at Corran,' says Dace, 'and the Lesser Instruments there buy anything that still ticks, and a few things that only used to.' He rolls his cord. 'Mister Lisle sells dreg to lens-grinders at Low Water by the pound. He says it takes the edge off a lens. He does not say off what.'".
  }
  Relation heardBeams(group).
  Topic wenu_beams with wenu "Ask Wenu about the chalk numbers on the roof beams" when true once {
    Says "'Eleven hundred and nine, and every one counted forty times,' says Wenu. 'Apprentices do it to stay awake. We keep a book on who finishes first. It is called the Beams Book and I have never lost a penny by it.' She lowers her voice. 'There is a beam in the middle, number six hundred and six, that has never been counted by the same person twice. Everyone gets a different number. Nobody will say what happens to the ones who count it right.'".
    On discuss { Assert heardBeams(party). }
  }

  // ---- The endings ----
  Ending the_front_door "The Front Door" when nemeFree(party) "Nobody in Cobble Ring was watching the sky, and so nobody saw a girl in a torn coat come down the last long stair of the Keel into Haddo's barley on the morning after the third night. The house in the field is glass now and nothing more; the doors are only doors, and they open where they are looked at. Kezu sleeps through the night and wakes at dawn like anyone, and the first thing she does is climb to the loft, and sit in the seat that has been Hanu's, and look at the room in the barley, and at the girl on the stool beside it with a dreg marble in her fist, and not look away. The council kept or sold the house as it did. It does not matter now. In the Keel, a lamp has gone out on the Slope, and an old woman has gone up the stair to see whether Wenn is in his bunk.".
  Ending the_chair "The Chair" when nemeSits(party) "Tobu sits in the child's chair in the middle of the Long Hall and counts forty doors, and the house does not grow. Neme goes down the stair into the Strewnfield with her coat buttoned wrong, and is looked after by Hanu, who has been a week without a patient and is glad of one. Kezu sleeps, and wakes, and goes to the hall every noon with a cup of something hot, and sits on the glass beside her sister's boy for an hour, not speaking, and goes home again. Cobble Ring does not speak of it, as a town does not speak of the stool it keeps empty for someone.".
  Ending the_gate_shut "The Knocking Goes On" when nemeLeft(party) "You went back up the Slope, as you had said you would, to see to your own affairs, and the gate shut behind you. The house goes on as it did. Kezu is walked back to her bed by Hanu every morning; the council meets; the barley is not sown. At the foot of the Slope an old woman minds a lamp for a boy called Wenn, and the knocking comes up the glass, and stops, and comes again. Some night it will be answered. Whether by someone who has been told is only a matter of who comes by.".
}
